Hi managers

I have two printers, an old oki80 line printer and a HP LaserJet 4200 
PCL6.  When printing ASCII files from the server, the oki80 inserts 
carriage returns and the printout is just as it is on screen.  The LaserJet 
by contrast seems to think the whole file is a single line, and so the top 
line vanishes off the right end of the first page, followed by the 
appropriate number of blank pages.

Is this correctable by tweaking /etc/printcap?  I found some pages on 
google suggesting the insertion of LF (linefeed) or FF (formfeed) in 
