Fellow Sysadmins,

I've got a question about heterogeneous environments. This question is =
not perhaps a pure Tru64 question but since I am trying to identify =
solutions for a Tru64 platform, I thought about trying this list first.

We run SAP applications like R/3 & CRM in a heterogeneous environment. =
The backend database servers are Tru64 & the application servers are =
Wintel. Since the Central Instance is on a UNIX server, the trans, =
global, profile & exe directories need to be shared with the Wintel =
application server via samba. It's somewhat disconcerting trying to =
support a mission critical application with an unsupported product like =
Samba. Upon investigation Advanced Server for UNIX was identified as a =
possible substitute product.

My questions are -

a. Is there anyone who is running SAP Application using Advanced Server =
for UNIX? If so, what are your experiences if you don't mind sharing =
them with us?

b. I noticed you can get Samba support from quite a few companies =
http://us1.samba.org/samba/support/us.html However, how does one pick a =
particular company to provide support for Samba from all these =
organizations? Is there anyone who is paying for Samba support and has =
good stories about their vendor? If so, can you please share them with =
us?

Any and all help will be greatly appreciated!

