Mary, Tom, Mohamed, Charles, Tige, Michael, and all, 

Once again thanks for the fast support, very commendable.   It seems that 
a pattern is developing, whenever I start working in depth on a problem, 
something happens and via the segway, I go down uncharted (for me) 
troubleshooting of the Tru64 creature.  Of what type I am not sure, could 
be bear, or at the least some kind of beast, I will give it a name in a 
year. 

When at the SRM prompt I did a boot, and that is when the fun really 
started.   Our company inherited these Alpha boxes on a contract change of 

ownership, and at some undetermined point, a drive failure occurred when 
the previous owners had the box.  And then today another drive failure 
happened.  Hence the RAID = DEAD message in the bios utility for the 
Adaptec.   Seems that a utility called    "StorageWorks Command Console" 
and its agent for Intel, is needed to give assurance that the Raid set is 
really working.   So in a nutshell, the recently acquired machine is going 

to be rebuilt with all loss of file structure, Oracle, user data, Java, 
........    Too bad the other company didn't have any tape devices 
working.

Have a good day.




Kevin McCarty
CCNP


