Thanks to Dr. Thomas Blinn for the solution:
  In my recollection, the XP1000 was not supported in V4.0E.  It is in
  V5.x, but you have an unsupported configuration because you have the
  CDROM drive connection to the second IDE port (dqb0) instead of to
  the primary port (dqa0).  The SCSI emulation logic for the IDE CDROM
  drive doesn't work right to boot from dqb0.  That's what the message
  you are getting means.  It has NOTHING to do with your SCSI hard disk
  and in fact the odds are excellent that the SCSI disk will work just
  fine once you move the IDE cable to the other connector on the system
  motherboard.

  I suspect Linux and the various BSD UNIX versions don't care about
  this, but Tru64 UNIX doesn't get it right, and it's never going to be
  fixed, so move the cable.

