Evening Managers,

Some really good news, after facing a rebuild after days of HP hardware 
and OS phone support, I decided to rebuild the system as per my morning 
email.  When I went to create a h_domain we use, I received a warning 
message that basically said I would lose data if I created the h_domain. A 
further clue was that when I did a customize option on the disk I noticed 
the same file structure as before ( the panic dump of root , yesterday) 
and after a few hundred keystrokes, voila !   Oracle is back and so is the 
several hundred thousand files that go with it. 

So the RAID5 rebuid after a controller burp didn't succeed in stopping the 
panic dump when vmunix, then root tried to load, but after an install, the 
recovery of the h_domain was possible with the   /advfs scan  toolsets and 
  the -r -f -q flags,  then renaming the generic domain_dsk0h to h_domain 
in /etc/fdmns  and remounting h_domain.    I think I got that right. 

What a learning experience.   Stressful but fun.   So what's next? 

All have a good day.

Kevin McCarty
CCNP


